decisions:
  - id: d-export-all-offscreen
    decision: Create fresh offscreen canvas + ImageCache per file in batch export
    rationale: Ensures clean state between exports, avoids image cache collisions between different documents
  - id: d-binary-endpoint
    decision: Add separate /api/export endpoint for binary writes
    rationale: Existing /api/file uses text encoding — binary export data (GIF/MP4/WebM blobs) needs raw Buffer handling
  - id: d-h264-candidates
    decision: Try H.264 High Profile levels 5.1/4.2/4.0 before Baseline 3.1
    rationale: Baseline 3.1 only supports 720p. Most keynote files are 1920x1080@60fps. Matches the multi-candidate pattern already used by WebM export
errors_encountered:
  - description: 'Export All: 0 exported, 50 failed — all files silently failed'
    resolution: Added error logging to catch block; root cause was MP4 codec profile too low for 1080p
    time_to_fix: 10min
  - description: H.264 codec not supported for 1920x1080 at 60fps
    resolution: Changed from single Baseline 3.1 codec to multi-candidate High Profile list
    time_to_fix: 5min
  - description: atelier --version showed 0.1.0 instead of actual version
    resolution: Replaced hardcoded string with createRequire reading package.json
    time_to_fix: 2min
learnings:
  - H.264 Baseline Profile Level 3.1 (avc1.42001f) maxes out at 720p — need High Profile for 1080p+
  - WebCodecs VideoEncoder.isConfigSupported() is the correct way to probe codec support before encoding
  - Turbo cache can serve stale builds after source changes — use --force flag when iterating quickly
  - Silent catch blocks in batch operations make debugging impossible — always log errors
